.TH APT-DOWNGRADE 1 "October 2026" "apt-downgrade 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apt-downgrade \- downgrade installed packages to a target version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt-downgrade
\fB\-\-current\fR \fIversion\fR
\fB\-\-downgrade\fR \fItarget\fR
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apt-downgrade
lists installed packages that match an exact version
(\fB\-\-current\fR), then proposes an
.B apt install
command pinning those packages to
.IR target .
.PP
Listing and
.B \-\-dry\-run
do not require root. Applying the install requires root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-current \fIversion\fR
Installed package version to match exactly.
.TP
.B \-\-downgrade \fItarget\fR
Target version for the generated apt install command.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show matching packages and the command without installing.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, cancellation by the user, or no matching packages.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, failed listing, failed confirmation read, missing root for install, or apt failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APT_DOWNGRADE_LANG
Force UI language (examples:
.BR en ,
.BR es ,
.BR pt_BR ,
.BR fr ,
.BR de ,
.BR zh_CN ,
.BR ja ).
If unset, the language follows
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
then
.BR LANG .
Unsupported locales fall back to English.
.TP
.B APT_DOWNGRADE_LIST_CMD
Override the command used to list installed packages (mainly for tests).
.TP
.B APT_DOWNGRADE_FORCE_NONROOT
If set to a non-empty value other than
.BR 0 ,
pretend the process is not root (used by automated tests in containers).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
apt\-downgrade \-\-current 1.2.3\-1 \-\-downgrade 1.0.0\-1 \-\-dry\-run
sudo apt\-downgrade \-\-current 1.2.3\-1 \-\-downgrade 1.0.0\-1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
